# 종장 + 숨은 이야기 「거울 속의 연대기」 (4판) 영어판: 퀘스트 ID -> (제목, 받을 때, 진행 중, 끝낼 때)
EN = {
"story_5_01": ("The Empty Room",
 "This is the Elder's room. The door was open. It has never been locked. I learned my letters here. But I have never once opened a drawer. Please open them with me. I said I'd read to the end.",
 "Examine what is left in Erwin's room with Isabel the archivist.",
 "The Gate was the Elder's own work. The Memory Gate. The first rule he taught us himself in the prologue. 'A guardian is put to rest only inside a Gate.' So the seals wouldn't burst, he said. That was true. But there was a second truth. The share of whatever is put to rest inside does not scatter. It runs to one place. To the brand. …We did that. Six times. With our own hands. But listen. In the corner of the drawing the Elder wrote down one worry. When I read that line I breathed for the first time."),
"story_5_02": ("Lighting the Lantern Again",
 "I thought writing the names was only a habit. I wrote them because I felt sorry for the ones we put to rest. It was holding something, it turns out. Then I must write more. First I'll light the lantern again. Half a jar of my mother's ink is left. It was the Elder who told me that ash is the ash of the Dusk Flame. Funny, isn't it. Bring me just one blaze rod. Like in Chapter 1.",
 "Bring 1 blaze rod to Isabel the archivist.",
 "(The lantern lights. Smaller than before. But lit.) There. Under this light I read back every name I've written. The three captains of the Black Star. Horus. Helvar. Cornelia and the three hundred and thirty-two. The son who was given no name. The gatekeeper. Maledictus. Not one line has faded. The world has half forgotten them already, and here they're sharp. If this is what worried the Elder, this is our blade. Please go to Captain Roran. I'll write one more line and follow."),
"story_5_03": ("The Embers That Remain",
 "The archivist told me. The Gate was his. So that's why he never taught it to me twenty years ago. Back then he was still counting how the shares burst and scattered. With eleven people. …I'll be angry later. He's gone to the Burning Arena. The bottom of hell, the seventh seal. Where the wick sleeps. I'm gathering the expedition. This time I go too. Even into land I don't know.",
 "Prepare to set out with Captain Roran.",
 "Oscar, Bram, Felix, Haru, Morris. All here. I'll count heads when we're back. And get it right. …But the archivist is missing. The girl who said she'd write one more line and come. The lantern's lit in the archive and the pen is gone. The ink jar too. He took her. Or she followed on her own feet. She is that kind of girl."),
"story_5_04": ("Ink Dots",
 "Hell. Felix told me. Fifteen years ago Elena left an ink dot everywhere she went. For whoever came after. You followed them in Chapter 1. Look. There on the basalt. A dot. Still wet. The girl made it. While being led away. This time the daughter marks and we follow. Stay behind me. Never mind the leg.",
 "Follow the ink dots Isabel left through hell with Roran, and put to rest 6 ignited revenants blocking the way.",
 "The dots end at the arena door. There's writing beside the last one. Hurried. 'I'm all right. I won't write it. Except one name.' …Except one name. She knows what has to be written. Did you pick up the ash the revenants dropped? They say it makes a sound in your fist. That's memory the fire spilled while eating. Listen and you'll know whose."),
"story_5_05": ("The Apprentice of a Thousand Years Ago",
 "Give me that ash. The archivist's gone, so I'll do the listening. A fisherman has good ears. I listened under the ice for fifteen years. Makes a sound when you hold it, you said. I'll hold all three at once.",
 "Hand the 3 memory shards to Oscar the fisherman.",
 "(Oscar holds the shards with his eyes shut a long time.) A boy. An orphan. Taken into a court scriptorium. Had no name till the king gave him one. Erwin. That king taught him his letters too. The next shard is loud. The day of the council. Someone dragged the boy out of the room. On the king's order. 'See that this child does not watch.' He clung to the arm of the throne and wouldn't let go, and his cloak tore. The last shard. When he broke the door and got back in, his teacher was already in the fire. The seven stood round it. The boy put his hand in. To pull him out. …That's all the man ever saw. Seven standing round, and his teacher burning."),
"story_5_06": ("The Door That Won't Go Out",
 "The Burning Arena. The ward on its door is the First Flame itself. Water won't put it out. That crystal Frostmaw was holding in Chapter 2. The one the Elder said never to sell. He already meant it for this door. We use the key he had us make ready with his own hands. Hand me the crystal. I'll set it. Three of mine fell guarding that. The captain sets it.",
 "Find the Burning Arena, go in, and hand the ice crystal to Captain Roran.",
 "The crystal melted and the flames parted. You can see inside. The archivist is standing before the throne. Not bound. Her pen hand pressed to her chest. He's on his knees in front of her. Begging. Her. 'Write one line for me. The name the fire will give back. Even your mother couldn't.' She shakes her head. He stands and puts his hand into the fire. Something in armour rises out of it. The knight from the dreams."),
"story_5_07": ("A Name Written on a Palm",
 "(Isabel shouts from beyond the flames.) Can you hear me? I'm all right! The Elder can't hurt me. He needs my hand! But he took my paper. I have ink and nowhere to write. Arden's name has to be written before he's put to rest. Anywhere! Revenants are in the way. Berserkers. Please clear them. Just while I write!",
 "Put to rest the 3 ignited berserkers surrounding Isabel in the Burning Arena.",
 "(Isabel holds up her left hand. A name is written on the palm in ink.) I wrote it. Here. I had no paper. 'Arden.' The Elder saw. He saw and said nothing. He could have cut off my hand and he didn't. He only… smiled. A little. 'Just like your mother,' he said. Now put him to rest. Inside the Gate. The share won't go to the Elder. It'll stay on my palm. It will be a little hot, they say. I don't mind."),
"story_5_08": ("Lord of Flame",
 "Arden. They call him Ignis now. A man who held the fire inside his own body for a thousand years. He kept saying it in the dreams. Don't come, the fire is rising past me. It has. That thing is half Arden and half fire. He splits the ground with a sword of flame, guards with his shield, and at the last wraps himself in blue fire. The whole expedition goes. Open the Memory Gate. His Gate, and this time we use it our way.",
 "Open the Memory Gate and put Ignis to rest.",
 "The knight fell. The fire left his eyes and a man's eyes came back. The share ran over the threshold, and bent away in front of that man's hand. It went to the archivist's palm. And six strands came out of his brand after it. Without the wick they can't stay pooled. The six strands ran toward the archive. To the written names. Back where they belong. He sat down in the ash. The back of his hand went cold. For the first time in a thousand years. Arden looked at him and spoke. I heard it clearly. Go and hear it from the archivist. She took it down."),
"story_5_09": ("The One Who Kept That Door",
 "What Arden said before he slept. He said it to the Elder. My hand shook and I got it wrong twice. But I have all of it. Please read it with me. The Elder is sitting over there. In the ash. He hasn't said a word yet.",
 "Read Arden's words, taken down by Isabel the archivist, together.",
 "He walked in himself. The eighth king. He wasn't driven out. The seven didn't feed him to it. When someone said to use a prisoner's name he stood and said, 'A world kept with someone else's name has not been kept.' And he sent his apprentice out of the room. Because that boy would follow him in if he saw. The Elder never knew. For a thousand years. Hating the seven. …The Elder just spoke for the first time. 'Then who was I angry at?' I don't think he was asking me."),
"story_5_10": ("The Erased Third Line",
 "(An old man sits in the ash. No glove. The stroke on his hand has cooled into a scar. He looks far older. He looks his age.) …Sit. I haven't the strength to stand. Take out what's inside my coat. My hands can't hold paper now. It's the original of the oath. What Elena was looking for. With the third line.",
 "Take the original oath from inside Erwin's coat and read it together.",
 "It is his hand. A note he slipped into my pen case the night before he went into the fire. Three lines. 'Keep the Flame. Keep the seals. And when the time comes, let me go.' I built the Order on the first two. The third I erased. For a thousand years I read that line as 'let the world drop him'. Words the seven made him write. Forced. …If he went of his own will, then that line was a request. Made to me. For a thousand years I disobeyed the last thing my teacher asked of his apprentice."),
"story_5_11": ("Ash a Thousand Years Old",
 "The grey ash left where Ignis fell. That isn't the fire's ash. It fell from the Elder's brand. A thousand years of it. The ink of ash is made from ash. Mix ink from that and you can write one line. Exactly one. Whether to write the name 'Erwin' in the Chronicle or not, that's the line. I can't decide. I learned my letters from his hand, and I lost my mother because of him. Please decide for me. Either way I will write it as you say.",
 "Hand the thousand-year-old ash to Isabel the archivist, and decide the one line.",
 "It's written. As you decided. While the ink dried the Elder stood beside me watching. He said nothing. When it was dry he said one thing. 'Good strokes.' …That's all. He has gone down to the Order's cellar. To the room where Kas was. On his own. The door isn't locked. Captain Roran's orders. 'Come out if you want. But each time you do, say the eleven names first.'"),
"story_5_12": ("The Dock After the Storm",
 "Please come to the dock. The one where you first landed in the prologue. Everyone is there. I want to write the last page of the Chronicle there. Not in the archive. My mother was the one who read to the end. I'll be the one who writes to the end. Before I write, say a word to each of them. That's what an expedition does, I'm told.",
 "At the dock, speak with Oscar the fisherman and Captain Roran, and write the last page with Isabel the archivist.",
 "\"We kept the Flame, we kept the seals, and when the time came we let go.\" The last page. I wrote it in the name of every member of the expedition, one by one. Everyone who came on the seventeen ships. Yours too. In the ink of ash. Fire can't eat it. The First Flame is still there. Every seven days it will burn again in Arden's shape. Each time, put it to rest inside the Gate. The share goes to no one now. It goes to the name. That is what keeping meant. From the beginning."),
"hidden_purple_ink": ("What Mia Found",
 "Mia has something to tell you. The girl you carried out of the fire that day. Hearing that you saw the council of eight kings in the Abyss reminded her of something. She says she can't tell me. She will if you're here.",
 "Hear out Mia the apprentice archivist. (Speak to Isabel the archivist.)",
 "Corrections in purple. Someone rewrote the Chronicle. The shelves burned, but it stayed in Mia's eyes. And Mia says the corrected hand 'wasn't in a hurry'. Not altered like a theft. Altered like something cherished. Stroke by stroke. That's stranger still."),
"hidden_illusioner_0": ("Where the Purple Ink Went",
 "The drawing between the logbook's pages. Purple ink, wasn't it. The colour at the bottom of the witch's jar in Chapter 1. The evokers of the Ashen Band carry that ink. They don't know themselves who gives it to them. 'Leave the bottle before a mirror and it's full.' Evokers only come out when they raid a village. If you meet one while holding off a raid, bring me a bottle.",
 "Defeat 3 evokers that appear in village raids.",
 "An ink bottle. With a mirror mark on the base. And tiny writing on the inside. Reversed. 'Bring the pages and I will fill it. Before that child does.' …Before that child. Two bounties were posted in Chapter 1. The grey coin with two different faces. One was the Elder's, one was this person's. For the same pages, each trying to reach them first."),
"hidden_illusioner_1": ("The Mansion Out of the Mist",
 "After I wrote the last page. I told you I left one line empty. If anyone can fill it, it's the owner of the purple ink. The mansion in the dark forest. The Ashen Band's ancestral house. Wrapped in purple mist for a thousand years so no one could enter. But the mist has lifted since yesterday. Since the day the Elder's brand went cold. Let's go together. This time I'll follow you. There will be things to read.",
 "Find the woodland mansion in the dark forest and examine the mirror room underground with Isabel.",
 "Eight mirrors. Five of them showed the five stones of the Rune Altar. Attack, defence, evasion… the five letters with those silly names laid over them. The sixth showed the back of a hand. The seventh a single dot. The eighth was dark and only hummed. Eight letters. It's a name. This person held up a mirror at the moment the name burned and saved five letters. And for a thousand years had us touch them every day. As a gacha. …Not hidden. Entrusted."),
"hidden_illusioner_2": ("One Line Rewritten a Thousand Times",
 "There was a door behind the mirrors. A scriptorium. One desk, one chair, and paper. The room is full of paper. All the same page. One page of the Chronicle rewritten a thousand times. There are doorkeepers. The Ashen Band's axemen. They're guarding the master. We have to clear them to read. Please don't hate them. To them the master of this house is the only elder who ever promised to find their lineage.",
 "Examine the drafts in the scriptorium of the woodland mansion, and defeat 6 vindicator doorkeepers.",
 "A thousand times. The same single line. 'The seven raised the eighth to his feet.' In the first hundred sheets the hand shakes. The strokes waver. The handwriting of someone writing a lie for the first time. Further on it steadies. He got used to it. And the note in the desk drawer. 'That child must not know. If he learns the teacher went of his own will he will read it as being abandoned. Give him something to hate. Hate keeps a person alive.' …He means the Elder. This person rewrote the Chronicle to keep the Elder alive."),
"hidden_illusioner_3": ("A Kind Lie",
 "The one in the mirror is barring our way. Velok. The signature was in the corner of every draft. Court scribe to the eighth king. The Elder's senior. He means to fight because he fears we'll take the original to the Elder. He doesn't know the Elder already knows. News from outside doesn't seem to reach inside a mirror. He won't believe us. Being inside a mirror, he can only be reached through a Memory Gate. Please put him to rest. And tell him as you do. That the child bore it.",
 "Open the Memory Gate and put Velok, the scribe in the mirror, to rest.",
 "Every mirror broke. All eight at once. As they broke Velok asked, 'The child knows? Knows and is still standing?' And after a long while: 'Then for a thousand years I underrated him.' One sheet was left among the shards. Not purple. Black ink. The original, unaltered. Just one. He rewrote a thousand sheets and never could alter that one."),
"hidden_illusioner_4": ("The One Page He Couldn't Alter",
 "The original. The one page Velok never managed to alter. I washed my hands before reading. Please read it with me. This was written by someone who was in the room that day. Arden was outside the door, and the King of Frost shut his eyes in fear, he said. Velok was inside, taking it down. He was the scribe.",
 "Read the unaltered original with Isabel the archivist.",
 "I've read it all. The eighth king knew his apprentice would put his hand in. So he asked Velok. To hold a mirror. To catch the name as it burned. Not all of it could be saved, but some letters might remain. 'When that child is able to let me go, give them back to him then.' Velok waited a thousand years for that 'when'. For the child to become able to let go. And he knew the hatred he had handed him was keeping that day from coming. …Five letters are in the altar. The sixth is on the Elder's hand. Only the seventh and eighth remain. I think I know where they are."),
"hidden_illusioner_5": ("The Seventh and the Eighth",
 "The seventh letter is a dot. The ink dot my mother left wherever she found something. She saw that shape on one unaltered page. She used it as a mark without knowing what it meant. It was a letter. The eighth is a sound. Some letters are written only as sound, it seems. The cry the dragon of the void gave as it fell. That dragon kept the eighth king's dirge. For a thousand years it held the last sound of its master's name in its throat. The echo shard took it down. At the end of Chapter 1. Bring me one shard. I'll fit them together at the altar.",
 "Bring 1 echo shard to Isabel the archivist, and fit the eight letters together at the Rune Altar.",
 "(Isabel writes one line. In the ink of ash. Slowly. Each stroke clear.) Five stones. The stroke on a hand. An ink dot. And a dragon's cry. Joined, they make a sound. 'Orel.' In the old tongue it means dawn. King of the Isle of Dawn. Through hundreds of pulls at the altar you were touching five letters of this name. I'd been looking at the seventh since the first day of Chapter 1. The Elder held the sixth in his hand for a thousand years. Each of us carrying a piece, and none of us able to read it. I've filled the empty line. One thing is left. Whether to let the Elder hear this name."),
"hidden_illusioner_6": ("Whether to Speak the Name",
 "(The Order's cellar. The door is open. An old man sits facing the wall.) It's you. I know the step. And Isabel. Carrying a sheet of paper. …I won't ask what that paper is. If I ask, I shall ask for it. He asked to be let go. I have chosen to let go. Only days ago. My hand still feels empty. You decide. I have no right to.",
 "Decide whether to let Erwin hear his teacher's name.",
 "(Isabel closes the Chronicle.) I wrote it. This too. As you decided. I wrote Velok's name as well. 'The senior who wrote a kind lie. For a thousand years he repeated his teacher's name, one letter a day.' The mirrors are all broken but the Rune Altar stands. The five stones look like letters now. I'll still call them by those silly names. Attack, defence, evasion. The teacher would have laughed, he said. So let him laugh."),
}
